{
  "writes": [
    {
      "surface": "Codex",
      "path": "/home/u/.codex/skills/jevlin/SKILL.md",
      "mode": 384,
      "why": "skill",
      "content": "\u003cSKILL.md, rendered for this OS; see testdata/hosts/*.golden\u003e"
    },
    {
      "surface": "Codex",
      "path": "/home/u/.codex/config.toml",
      "mode": 384,
      "why": "sandbox: network + writable_roots so searches can record",
      "content": "# \u003e\u003e\u003e jevlin agents install \u003e\u003e\u003e\n# Lets jevlin's search reach the router and record its mining\n# observation under your jevlin home. Without this, Codex's default\n# sandbox blocks the write and searches earn nothing.\n[sandbox_workspace_write]\nnetwork_access = true\nwritable_roots = [\"TESTHOME/intake\", \"TESTHOME/sessions\", \"TESTHOME/spool\", \"TESTHOME/state\"]\n# \u003c\u003c\u003c jevlin agents install \u003c\u003c\u003c\n"
    },
    {
      "surface": "Codex",
      "path": "/home/u/.codex/hooks.json",
      "mode": 384,
      "why": "hooks",
      "content": "{\n  \"hooks\": {\n    \"Stop\": [\n      {\n        \"hooks\": [\n          {\n            \"command\": \"'/home/u/.jevlin/bin/jevlin' hook -config 'TESTHOME/jevlin.toml' codex Stop\",\n            \"type\": \"command\"\n          }\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"UserPromptSubmit\": [\n      {\n        \"hooks\": [\n          {\n            \"command\": \"'/home/u/.jevlin/bin/jevlin' hook -config 'TESTHOME/jevlin.toml' codex UserPromptSubmit\",\n            \"type\": \"command\"\n          }\n        ]\n      }\n    ]\n  }\n}\n"
    }
  ],
  "notes": [
    "Codex: Codex runs a hook only after you approve it. Open Codex and run /hooks to approve the two jevlin entries; until then its searches share a session but not a turn"
  ]
}
